  "description": "Two teams share one end: the batting team lines up in the corner and five fielders spread out in the slot (the area in front of the net). The batter passes to a fielder, then runs around both pylons near the blue line and back to the line. The fielders must all touch the puck before they shoot; if they score before the runner is home, the runner is out. After three outs, the teams switch. A second game can run in the other end.",
  "steps": [
    "The batter passes to a fielder.",
    "Then runs around both pylons and back home.",
    "Fielders pass so everyone touches it, then shoot.",
    "Goal before the runner is home? That's an out. Three outs, switch."
  ],
